# `pluss::subsp::stats::ts::ljung_box`

The Ljung–Box test that a series, or a model's residuals, is white noise up to a set of lags.

## Signature

```cpp
ts::LjungBoxResult ts::ljung_box(const pluss::Series& x, const ts::LjungBoxOptions& options = {}, pluss::codem::Config cfg = {});
```

## What It Does

`ljung_box` tests the null hypothesis that the autocorrelations of `x` at lags `1 … m` are all zero, for each `m` in `options.lags`. The statistic is `Q = n (n + 2) Σ r[k]² / (n − k)`, compared with a chi-squared distribution whose degrees of freedom are `m − model_df`. A small p-value says the series is not white noise.

When `x` is the residual series of a fitted ARMA model, set `model_df` to the number of ARMA coefficients that were estimated: the residuals of a fitted model are slightly more regular than white noise and the degrees of freedom must be reduced accordingly. Without it the test is too lenient.

## Parameters

`const pluss::Series& x`
: A one-dimensional series in time order, at least two observations long.

`const ts::LjungBoxOptions& options`
: `lags` (the lag sets to test, default {10}), `model_df` (degrees of freedom to subtract, default 0), `norm` and `demean`; see [`LjungBoxOptions`](LjungBoxOptions.md).

`pluss::codem::Config cfg`
: Output configuration (dtype and platform of the returned series); the computation itself runs in double precision.

## Returns

A [`LjungBoxResult`](LjungBoxResult.md) with one entry per element of `options.lags`: the lags, the statistics, the p-values and the degrees of freedom, each a `Series`.

## Errors

- `lags` must not be empty.
- `model_df` must leave positive degrees of freedom at every lag.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

An autoregressive series is far from white noise at lags 5, 10 and 20.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>

#include <cmath>
#include <iomanip>
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

const auto f64 = pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float64);
void show(const char* label, const Series& s) {
  std::cout << std::left << std::setw(14) << label << std::right << std::fixed << std::setprecision(4);
  for (double v : s.host<double>()) std::cout << std::setw(9) << v;
  std::cout << "\n";
}
std::vector<double> noise(int n) {
  std::vector<double> e(n);
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    double u = std::sin(12.9898 * (i + 1.0) + 78.233) * 43758.5453;
    u -= std::floor(u);
    e[i] = u - 0.5;
  }
  return e;
}
Series ar1(int n, double phi) {
  const auto e = noise(n);
  std::vector<double> x(n);
  double carry = 0.0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    carry = phi * carry + e[i];
    x[i] = carry;
  }
  return pluss::make_series(x, {n}, f64);
}
Series walk(int n) {
  const auto e = noise(n);
  std::vector<double> x(n);
  double sum = 0.0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    sum += e[i];
    x[i] = sum;
  }
  return pluss::make_series(x, {n}, f64);
}

int main() {
  const Series y = ar1(200, 0.7);
  ts::LjungBoxOptions options;
  options.lags = {5, 10, 20};
  const auto test = ts::ljung_box(y, options);
  show("lags", test.lags);
  show("statistic", test.stat);
  show("dof", test.dof);
  std::cout << std::scientific << std::setprecision(2);
  for (double p : test.pvalue.host<double>()) std::cout << "p-value " << p << "\n";
}
```

### Example 2

Noise that has no dependence is not rejected.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>

#include <cmath>
#include <iomanip>
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

const auto f64 = pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float64);
void show(const char* label, const Series& s) {
  std::cout << std::left << std::setw(14) << label << std::right << std::fixed << std::setprecision(4);
  for (double v : s.host<double>()) std::cout << std::setw(9) << v;
  std::cout << "\n";
}
std::vector<double> noise(int n) {
  std::vector<double> e(n);
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    double u = std::sin(12.9898 * (i + 1.0) + 78.233) * 43758.5453;
    u -= std::floor(u);
    e[i] = u - 0.5;
  }
  return e;
}
Series ar1(int n, double phi) {
  const auto e = noise(n);
  std::vector<double> x(n);
  double carry = 0.0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    carry = phi * carry + e[i];
    x[i] = carry;
  }
  return pluss::make_series(x, {n}, f64);
}
Series walk(int n) {
  const auto e = noise(n);
  std::vector<double> x(n);
  double sum = 0.0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    sum += e[i];
    x[i] = sum;
  }
  return pluss::make_series(x, {n}, f64);
}

int main() {
  const Series y = pluss::make_series(noise(200), {200}, f64);
  const auto test = ts::ljung_box(y);
  std::cout << std::fixed << std::setprecision(4) << "statistic " << test.stat.host<double>()[0] << ", p-value " << test.pvalue.host<double>()[0] << "\n";
}
```

### Example 3

`model_df` removes degrees of freedom for the coefficients of a fitted model: 10 lags and 2 fitted coefficients leave 8.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>

#include <cmath>
#include <iomanip>
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

namespace ts = pluss::subsp::stats::ts;
using pluss::Series;

const auto f64 = pluss::Config{}.with_dtype(pluss::ScalarType::Float64);
void show(const char* label, const Series& s) {
  std::cout << std::left << std::setw(14) << label << std::right << std::fixed << std::setprecision(4);
  for (double v : s.host<double>()) std::cout << std::setw(9) << v;
  std::cout << "\n";
}
std::vector<double> noise(int n) {
  std::vector<double> e(n);
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    double u = std::sin(12.9898 * (i + 1.0) + 78.233) * 43758.5453;
    u -= std::floor(u);
    e[i] = u - 0.5;
  }
  return e;
}
Series ar1(int n, double phi) {
  const auto e = noise(n);
  std::vector<double> x(n);
  double carry = 0.0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    carry = phi * carry + e[i];
    x[i] = carry;
  }
  return pluss::make_series(x, {n}, f64);
}
Series walk(int n) {
  const auto e = noise(n);
  std::vector<double> x(n);
  double sum = 0.0;
  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    sum += e[i];
    x[i] = sum;
  }
  return pluss::make_series(x, {n}, f64);
}

int main() {
  const Series y = ar1(200, 0.7);
  ts::LjungBoxOptions options;
  options.lags = {10};
  options.model_df = 2;
  show("dof", ts::ljung_box(y, options).dof);
}
```


